"The confirmation step carries several rules. The branch, scheme, semester and academic year must all be present in the upload metadata. The confirmer must be permitted to write in the branch named in the metadata; the branch is a filter and never a grant. Students are resolved by roll number within branch and year, because a roll number is unique only inside that pair, and resolving across the college would attach a mark to the wrong candidate. The subject's configured maximum overrides the parser's default, and an over-maximum mark is reported and skipped rather than written, because such a value would corrupt every percentage derived from it. A row for a subject the teacher is not allocated to is skipped and listed rather than rejected, because a statement commonly covers the entire class and the upload should still complete with the skipped rows visible. Re-confirming an already-confirmed upload updates rather than duplicates, because the write is keyed on the student, offering, component and year together. All writes in one confirmation occur in a single transaction, and row-level problems are collected with their reasons and presented together rather than raised as exceptions, so a single bad row does not discard the remainder of an otherwise sound extraction.",
